# Private keys and secrets must NEVER be committed — anything pushed to GitHub is public,
# and a leaked key can't be un-leaked, only replaced. Secrets belong in Vercel's
# Environment Variables instead. See the Isar Obsidian note "Security lockdown".
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
.env
.env.*

# Local junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
node_modules/
.vercel
